  "description": "The SSL service group **sg1** (service name **svc1**) is currently configured to use a trusted CA (enabled) and to redirect clients with weak ciphers to **https://example.com/cipher**. Plain HTTP traffic is accepted on clear\u2011text port **80**, while the Common Name presented to peers is **www.example.com**. Client authentication is turned off, but the service will accept optional client certificates. Certificate revocation checking via CRL is mandatory, and OCSP checking is optional; however, OCSP stapling has been enabled to improve handshake efficiency.  \n\nDiffie\u2011Hellman support is enabled, using the parameter file **/etc/ssl/dhparams.pem** with a key\u2011exchange count of **5** and the key\u2011exchange size limit disabled. Export\u2011RSA (ERSA) is disabled, though the ERSA count is set to **10**. Non\u2011FIPS ciphers are permitted, and strict signature\u2011digest checking is enforced. The configuration disables redirect\u2011port rewriting, sets **sendCloseNotify** to **YES**, and enables server authentication. Session reuse is enabled with a timeout of **300\u202fseconds**. SNI is disabled and no SNI certificate is used. SSL\u202f2.0 is disabled while SSL\u202f3.0 is enabled; the SSL profile in use is **defaultSSLProfile**. Both SSL redirect and SSLv2 redirect are disabled, with the SSLv2 fallback URL pointing to **https://example.com/sslv2**. Finally, TLS\u202f1.0, TLS\u202f1.1, TLS\u202f1.2 and TLS\u202f1.3 are all enabled."
